From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Williams <awillia@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:25:42 -0700
Subject: gpu: Ignore client unpack geometry on compressed texture uploads

Per OpenGL ES 3.2, "All pixel storage modes are ignored when decoding a
compressed texture image" (sec. 8.7; sec. 8.4.1 scopes unpack state to
TexImage*, TexSubImage*, and ReadPixels only). With a
PIXEL_UNPACK_BUFFER bound, however, the validating decoder leaves
renderer-supplied UNPACK_ROW_LENGTH / UNPACK_IMAGE_HEIGHT values
resident in the real driver across compressed uploads, and some drivers
consume them there, causing bad reads relative to the bound buffer.

Add ScopedCompressedUnpackStateScrub, which resets the two values to the
ES defaults around every compressed dispatch in the validating decoder
(DoCompressedTexImage, DoCompressedTexSubImage, and the
ClearCompressedTextureLevel paths, which upload CPU-sourced data while
the client's values are still resident) and restores the tracked values
afterwards via ContextState::UpdateUnpackParameters(). Conformant
drivers cannot observe the change, and client-visible unpack state is
unchanged. This matches what ANGLE has done at its compressed entry
points since crrev.com/c/3296622, so the passthrough decoder already
behaves this way.

Bug: 562279351
Change-Id: I86cc40508da104089166de631f07c4674b586825
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8419890
Commit-Queue: Andrew Williams <awillia@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702241}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
ClearCompressedTextureLevel()/ClearCompressedTextureLevel3D() on this
branch do not have the
LOCAL_COPY_REAL_GL_ERRORS_TO_WRAPPER/LOCAL_PEEK_GL_ERROR error
propagation from a later upstream change, so only the
ScopedCompressedUnpackStateScrub lines were inserted there.

